<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Isolated protection posted.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Isolated protection posted.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Isolated two cents a bushel protection on hard red winter wheat was posted Monday as the continued rapid pace of harvesting and reports of high yields weighed on values and was expected to depress KCBT HRW wheat futures, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>They noted yields appeared to be improving from already high levels as the harvest moved into northern Kansas.</p>
<p>Basis bids were steady to weak, weighed down by harvest pressure although many farmers remained reluctant to sell at prices which in some areas are below $3.00 a bushel.</p>
<p>&quot;Sales have been on the slow side but deliveries have been good,&quot; one Oklahoma dealer said.  </p>
